  "id": "COMPOUND:17246 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between CID 11603911 and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, through a series of target interactions involving microtubule-associated protein 1B. CID 11603911 is directly targeting microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 6-hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, oleamide, and (4S,4aR,5S,8aR,9aS)-4a,5,6,7,8,8a,9,9a-Octahydro-4-hydroxy-9a-methoxy-3,4a,5-trimethylnaphtho(2,3-b)furan-2(4H)-one. These compounds all act as targets for the SDR family member 9, indicating a common pathway of action. The consistent presence of microtubule-associated protein 1B as a central node in the target network supports the idea that CID 11603911 may inhibit this protein, thereby affecting the SDR family member 9. The evidence is robust, with multiple independent pathways converging on the same target, suggesting a well-defined mechanism of action. The integration of these findings implies that CID 11603911 may exert its effects through a pathway involving microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn interacts with the SDR family member 9, potentially modulating its activity.",
